      en: "Buffalo Hill (337 m) is a hill in Ma On Shan Country Park, New Territories. Its name derives from its buffalo-like shape. Composed of granite and metamorphic schist, it is part of the Ma On Shan Hiking Trail. The hill hosts rare flora such as the Hong Kong orchid (Dendrobium candidum). Freshwater crabs inhabit the streams. From the summit, views extend across Tolo Harbour and the Ping Chau islands. During the Ming dynasty (1368–1644), coal was mined on the hill; remnants of adits remain visible. The average annual temperature is 23 °C. Buffalo Hill is popular for family hikes and birdwatching, with over 100 bird species recorded.",
